### 2. Update the Frontend (VoucherPostingStatus.js)
Now that the backend is sending the pre-formatted string (e.g., "1h 15m"), we just need to capture it and display it in the view modal.
**Step A: Add the State Variable**
Find your existing state variables at the top of the component and add one for the new time string:
```javascript
  const [viewingBatchRequestCount, setViewingBatchRequestCount] = useState(0);
  // Add this directly below the line above:
  const [viewingBatchTimeSinceLastAction, setViewingBatchTimeSinceLastAction] = useState("");

```
**Step B: Capture the String on Modal Open**
Find the handleOpenViewModal function and update it to pull the string from the selected row:
```javascript
  const handleOpenViewModal = async (row) => {
    setViewingBatchId(row.batchId);
    setViewingBatchCreatorId(row.creatorId);
    setViewingBatchState(row.currentStatus || "");
    setViewingBatchRawStatus(row.batchStatus || "");
    setViewingBatchRequestDate(row.requestDate);
    setViewingBatchRequestCount(row.requestCount || 0);
    setViewingBatchOrder(row.currentOrder);
    
    // Add this line to capture the backend time string:
    setViewingBatchTimeSinceLastAction(row.timeSinceLastAction || "");

```
